# ONE LINE PER IMPLEMENTATION: name, operations passed, then one cell per
# operation in the order run,runlots,add,update,select,swaprows,remove,clear.
#   ok  the specified assertion held      XX  it did not
#   --  NOPRE: a previous operation left the precondition unmet (a cascade)
#   TMO the run did not finish (see TIMEOUT in jsfb_matrix.py -- the only
#       verdict here that depends on the clock, and the only one that can flap)
#
# THE FIRST TWO LINES ARE THE CONTROLS AND THEY ARE NOT ROWS.
#   control 0                the null control -- the reference implementation's
#                            own index.html with its <script> elements deleted.
#                            jsfb_matrix.py refuses to print a matrix if it is
#                            not 0, so a baseline saying otherwise could not
#                            have been produced by that program.
#   control-static-run FAIL  the SECOND control, added 2026-08-28 because the
#                            first cannot see the hole it covers: `rows==1000
#                            afterwards` is also true of a page BORN with 1,000
#                            rows that ignored the click. That page is built
#                            here, binds no handler, and `run` must FAIL on it.
#                            Watched in both directions -- with the pre-fix
#                            count-only assertion it reports PASS and the
#                            matrix refuses.
#
# NOTE THAT `keyed/no-js` IS NOT A CONTROL, despite its name and despite what
# any dispatch may say. It is No.JS v1.20.0, a 136 KB HTML-first reactive
# framework (src/no.js, MIT, no-js.dev) whose src/main.js registers three
# globals with it. Its score is a finding about this browser, not a control
# firing, and reading it as a control would retire a real defect silently.
